\mt1 2 Thessalonians
\c 1
\s1 Greetings to the Thessalonians
\r (\ref 1 Thessalonians 1:1–10|1TH 1:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 1 Paul, Silvanus,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft That is, Silas\f* and Timothy,
\p To the church of \add the\add* Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:
\p \v 2 Grace and peace to you from God our Father\f + \fr 1:2 \ft SBL, NE, and WH \fqa God the Father\f* and the Lord Jesus Christ.
\p \v 3 We are obligated to thank God for you all the time, brothers, as is fitting, because your faith is growing more and more, and your love for one another is increasing. \v 4 That is why we boast among God’s churches about your perseverance and faith in the face of all \add the\add* persecution and affliction you are enduring.
\s1 Christ’s Coming
\p \v 5  \add All this is \add* clear evidence of God’s righteous judgment. And so you will be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are suffering. \v 6 After all, \add it is\add* only right for God to repay with affliction those who afflict you, \v 7 and to grant relief to you who are oppressed and to us \add as well\add*. \add This will take place when\add* the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with His mighty angels \v 8 in blazing fire, inflicting vengeance on those who do not know God and do not obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus. \v 9 \add They\add* will suffer \add the\add* penalty of eternal destruction, separated from \add the\add* presence of the Lord and the glory of His might, \v 10 on \add the\add* day He comes to be glorified in His saints and regarded with wonder by all who have believed, including you who have believed our testimony.
\p \v 11 To this end, we always pray for you, that our God will count you worthy of \add His\add* calling, and \add that\add* He will powerfully fulfill \add your\add* every good desire and work of faith, \v 12 so that the name of our Lord Jesus will be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and of \add the\add* Lord Jesus Christ.\f + \fr 1:12 \ft Or \fqa the grace of our God and Lord, Jesus Christ.\f*
\c 2
\s1 The Man of Lawlessness
\p \v 1 Now concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our being gathered together to Him, we ask you, brothers, \v 2 not to be easily disconcerted \add or\add* alarmed by \add any\add* spirit \add or\add* message \add or\add* letter seeming \add to be\add* from us, \add alleging\add* that the Day of the Lord has already come. \v 3 \add Let\add* no one deceive you in \add any\add* way, for \add it will not come \add* until the rebellion occurs and the man of lawlessness — the son of destruction — is revealed. \v 4 \add He\add* will oppose and exalt himself above every so-called god or object of worship. So he will seat himself in the temple of God, proclaiming himself to be God.
\p \v 5 Do you not remember that I told you these things while I was still with you? \v 6 And you know what is now restraining \add him\add*, so that he may be revealed at the proper time. \v 7 For the mystery of lawlessness \add is\add* already at work, but the \add one who\add* now restrains \add it will continue\add* until he is taken out of \add the\add* way. \v 8 And then the lawless \add one\add* will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus will slay with the breath of His mouth and annihilate by the majesty of His arrival.
\p \v 9 The coming \add of the lawless one\add* will be accompanied by \add the\add* working of Satan, with every kind of power, sign, and false wonder, \v 10 and with every wicked deception directed against those who are perishing, because they refused the love of the truth that would have saved them. \v 11 For this reason God will send them a powerful delusion so that they believe \add the\add* lie, \v 12 in order that judgment may come upon all who have disbelieved the truth \add and\add* delighted in wickedness.
\s1 Stand Firm
\p \v 13 But we should always thank God for you, brothers who are loved by \add the\add* Lord, because God chose you from \add the\add* beginning\f + \fr 2:13 \ft Or \fqa God has chosen you as the firstfruits\f* to be saved by \add the\add* sanctification of \add the\add* Spirit and \add by\add* faith in \add the\add* truth. \v 14 To this He called you through our gospel, so that you may share in \add the\add* glory of our Lord Jesus Christ. \v 15 Therefore, brothers, stand firm and cling to the traditions we taught you, whether by speech or by letter.
\p \v 16 Now \add may\add* our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father, who by grace has loved us and given \add us\add* eternal comfort and good hope, \v 17 encourage your hearts and strengthen \add you\add* in every good word and deed.
\c 3
\s1 Request for Prayer
\p \v 1 Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may spread quickly and be held in honor, just as \add it was\add* with you. \v 2 And \add pray\add* that we may be delivered from wicked and evil men; for not everyone \add holds to \add* the faith. \v 3 But the Lord is faithful, \add and He\add* will strengthen \add you\add* and guard you from the evil \add one\add*.\f + \fr 3:3 \ft Or \fqa from evil\f* \v 4 And we have confidence in \add the\add* Lord that you are doing and will continue to do what we command. \v 5 \add May\add* the Lord direct your hearts into God’s love and Christ’s perseverance.
\s1 A Warning against Idleness
\p \v 6 Now we command you, brothers, in \add the\add* name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother \add who\add* leads an undisciplined life \add that is\add* not in keeping with the tradition you received\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Or \fqa they received\f* from us. \v 7 For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you, \v 8 nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you. \v 9 Not that we lack \add this\add* right, but we wanted to offer ourselves \add as\add* an example for you to imitate. \v 10 For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”
\p \v 11 For we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives, accomplishing nothing, but being busybodies. \v 12 We command and urge such \add people\add* by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living. \v 13 But \add as for\add* you, brothers, \add do\add* not grow weary \add in\add* well-doing.
\p \v 14 Take note of anyone who \add does\add* not obey the instructions we have given in \add this\add* letter. \add Do\add* not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed. \v 15 Yet \add do\add* not regard \add him\add* as an enemy, but admonish \add him\add* as a brother.
\s1 Signature and Final Greetings
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 16:19–24|1CO 16:19-24\ref*; \ref Colossians 4:15–18|COL 4:15-18\ref*)
\p \v 16 Now \add may\add* the Lord of peace Himself give you peace at all \add times and\add* in every way. The Lord \add be\add* with all of you.
\p \v 17 \add This\add* greeting \add is\add* in my own hand — Paul. This is \add my\add* mark in every letter; it is the way I write.
\p \v 18 The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ \add be\add* with all of you.\f + \fr 3:18 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
